-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests: the statuses s 335 reads, derived from facts and fed to row IL-08's s 335. Row IL-33.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from s 335 (lines 3611-3620) and the statuses before the run;
-- the working is beside each group. Day: 15 January 2026. The retirement age of a woman born in 1956
-- or later is the Retirement Age Law's (row IL-27's module), so the default readings answer.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Fixtures`

avi MEANS `an Israeli employee` "Avi" `born` (YMD 1988 3 10) `who is` `male`
batya MEANS `a person` "Batya" `born` (YMD 1990 6 20) `who is` `female` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1990 6 20)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`
visitor MEANS `a man living in Israel under` `a visitor's visa and licence of type B/1, B/2, B/3 or B/4, under regulation 5 of the Entry Regulations`
married MEANS `A woman's marriage` WITH `marital status` IS `married`, `her spouse's traces have vanished for two years` IS FALSE, `her spouse has been abroad for two years without her consent and has not supported her in that time` IS FALSE
widowed MEANS `A woman's marriage` WITH `marital status` IS `widowed`, `her spouse's traces have vanished for two years` IS FALSE, `her spouse has been abroad for two years without her consent and has not supported her in that time` IS FALSE
noPension MEANS `A widow's pension fact` WITH `entitled to a pension under section 132(1) to (5) or section 252` IS FALSE
pension MEANS `A widow's pension fact` WITH `entitled to a pension under section 132(1) to (5) or section 252` IS TRUE
-- A widowing long enough to count (married 2015, died 2020, a child, no separation).
aWidowing MEANS `A widowing` WITH `she was his wife at his death` IS TRUE, `the day of the marriage` IS YMD 2015 1 1, `the day of his death` IS YMD 2020 1 1, `she bore him a child` IS TRUE, `in the five years before his death she was separated from him for three years or more, including the twelve months before his death` IS FALSE, `she was entitled to maintenance from him by a judgment or a written agreement` IS FALSE, `he did in fact bear her maintenance in the twelve months before his death` IS TRUE, `a dependants' supplement was paid for her at his death under section 200 or 244` IS FALSE

rdDefault MEANS `the readings this row takes`

§ `Tests — the derived record (the thirteen fields of IL-08's record)`

-- Avi: a resident employee. Every field TRUE but the housewife, the widow pensioner and the controlling
-- shareholder.
#ASSERT (`s 335 — the statuses of` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `the calendar year of the period` EQUALS 2026
#ASSERT (`s 335 — the statuses of` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `an employee or a self-employed person`
#ASSERT (`s 335 — the statuses of` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `an Israeli resident`
#ASSERT (`s 335 — the statuses of` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `insured under Chapter 11`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 335 — the statuses of` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `a housewife as defined in section 238`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 335 — the statuses of` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `a widow pensioner as defined in section 238`
#ASSERT (`s 335 — the statuses of` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `insured under Chapter 5`
#ASSERT (`s 335 — the statuses of` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `insured under Chapter 6`
#ASSERT (`s 335 — the statuses of` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `insured under paragraph (1) of the definition of insured in section 158`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 335 — the statuses of` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company`
#ASSERT (`s 335 — the statuses of` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `an employee insured under Chapter 8`
#ASSERT (`s 335 — the statuses of` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `insured under Chapter 9`
#ASSERT (`s 335 — the statuses of` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `insured for long-term care`

§ `Tests — the branches s 335 puts together from those statuses`

-- Avi, in Schedule J's order: (a) not (he is a resident), but (i) imposes maternity on one insured under
-- Chapter 11 who is not a housewife or widow pensioner: maternity; (b) children (Ch 11, not a housewife);
-- (c) work injury (Ch 5); (d) accident injury (Ch 6); (e) unemployment (s 158(1), not controlling); (f) insolvency
-- (Ch 8 worker, not controlling); (g) disability (Ch 9); (h) long-term care; (i) senior citizens and survivors.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches in which contributions are payable, from the facts of` avi `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault EQUALS LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`, `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`, `disability`, `long-term care`, `senior citizens and survivors`

-- Batya, a housewife (married to Avi, does not work): Ch 11 insured but a housewife, so (b) and (i) leave her
-- out (and with them maternity and children); she is not an employee (no Ch 5, no s 158(1), no Ch 8);
-- she is insured under Chapter 6 and Chapter 9 (a resident of 35) and for long-term care (Chapter 11):
-- accident injury, disability, long-term care.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches in which contributions are payable, from the facts of` batya `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault EQUALS LIST `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`
-- A visitor on a B visa who works in Israel as an employee, not a resident: (a) imposes maternity (an employee
-- who is not a resident); Chapter 5 insures him (work injury); he is a worker under Chapter 8 (insolvency);
-- he is not a resident so not under Chapters 6, 9, 11 or s 158(1), and not for long-term care.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches in which contributions are payable, from the facts of` visitor `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault EQUALS LIST `maternity`, `work injury`, `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`

-- A widow pensioner: a woman born 20 June 1990, not working, widowed (married 2015, died 2020, a child), with a
-- pension under s 252. Ch 11 insured; not a housewife (not married); a widow pensioner. (b) children: yes;
-- (i) senior citizens, survivors and maternity: not (the widow pensioner is left out); (d) accident, (g) disability and
-- (h) long-term care: yes.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches in which contributions are payable, from the facts of` batya `, her marriage` widowed `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` (JUST aWidowing) `, her widow's pension` pension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault EQUALS LIST `children`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`
-- The same widow without the pension: not a widow pensioner, so (i) imposes senior citizens and maternity.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches in which contributions are payable, from the facts of` batya `, her marriage` widowed `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` (JUST aWidowing) `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault EQUALS LIST `maternity`, `children`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`, `senior citizens and survivors`

-- A controlling shareholder in a closely-held company, an employee: s 6B takes him out of Chapters 7 and 8:
-- no unemployment and no insolvency branch; the rest as for Avi.
#ASSERT `s 335 — the branches in which contributions are payable, from the facts of` (avi `with the work` (`the work of an employee in Israel, controlling` TRUE `, kibbutz member` FALSE `, entitled to wages` TRUE `, police type` FALSE `, insured earlier` FALSE)) `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` NOTHING `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault EQUALS LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `disability`, `long-term care`, `senior citizens and survivors`

-- A resident housewife is, by s 240(a), insured under Chapter 11 (a resident of 18 or over), and is a housewife by
-- s 238: the derived record says both, and s 335 carves her out by name (above). NOTES.md section 6, finding 1.
#ASSERT (`s 335 — the statuses of` batya `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `insured under Chapter 11`
#ASSERT (`s 335 — the statuses of` batya `, her marriage` married `, her spouse` (JUST avi) `, her widowhood` NOTHING `, her widow's pension` noPension `, on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `, reading` rdDefault)'s `a housewife as defined in section 238`
